            <ArticleTitle>[Peridural opioid analgesia in the terminal stage of cancer. Indications--implementation--results].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The indications for the application of opioids near the spinal cord are presented and two groups of patients treated with pericutaneous and intracorporeal systems are reported. If indicated, this method offers the possibility of treating patients on an outpatient basis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
